WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.829
This is the Solid Suite.

2
00:00:01.829 --> 00:00:07.682
It has the everyday apps you would expect, for files, documents, tasks, calendars and contacts.

3
00:00:07.682 --> 00:00:10.146
The difference is where your data lives.

4
00:00:10.996 --> 00:00:17.200
Today, every app keeps its own copy of your data, on its own servers, under its own rules.

5
00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:18.854
Solid turns that around.

6
00:00:18.854 --> 00:00:23.404
Your data lives in a pod that you control, and apps ask to use it.

7
00:00:24.254 --> 00:00:26.688
You can sign in with any Solid pod provider.

8
00:00:26.688 --> 00:00:31.777
For this walkthrough, we'll use the built-in demo pod, which lives entirely in your browser.

9
00:00:32.629 --> 00:00:36.547
One click, and we're in, as Alice, a fictional demo user.

10
00:00:37.401 --> 00:00:39.423
Home is the front door to your pod.

11
00:00:39.423 --> 00:00:45.028
It shows what's stored there, sorted into everyday categories like documents, calendar and media.

12
00:00:45.878 --> 00:00:50.058
And it keeps one question in view at all times: who else can see this?

13
00:00:50.908 --> 00:00:52.996
Drive works the way you'd expect.

14
00:00:52.996 --> 00:00:56.159
Folders, uploads, search, and a list or grid view.

15
00:01:01.223 --> 00:01:06.996
Any file or folder can be shared, moved, starred, or renamed, with keyboard shortcuts for each.

16
00:01:07.848 --> 00:01:11.139
Files open in a preview, read straight from the pod.

17
00:01:12.612 --> 00:01:14.510
Docs is a full word processor.

18
00:01:14.510 --> 00:01:16.217
Let's start a new document.

19
00:01:23.772 --> 00:01:25.918
As you type, it saves to your pod.

20
00:01:25.918 --> 00:01:31.661
Not as a file locked inside one app, but as open, linked data that other apps can read too.

21
00:01:33.669 --> 00:01:40.199
Close the tab, come back on another device, and it's all still there, because it was never stored anywhere else.

22
00:01:41.049 --> 00:01:43.188
Tasks is a simple to-do list.

23
00:01:43.188 --> 00:01:45.254
Press Q anywhere to add one.

24
00:01:46.431 --> 00:01:47.381
Type naturally.

25
00:01:47.381 --> 00:01:51.368
Tasks picks up the word tomorrow and sets the due date for you.

26
00:01:55.275 --> 00:02:01.309
Calendar has day, week, month and agenda views, with separate calendars for personal and work.

27
00:02:02.159 --> 00:02:09.473
Contacts keeps your address book in the same pod, with labels, imports, and a tool that finds and merges duplicates.

28
00:02:10.324 --> 00:02:14.347
Photos, Music and Money are earlier, but they already run on the same pod.

29
00:02:15.198 --> 00:02:17.262
Your music library and playlists.

30
00:02:21.307 --> 00:02:24.807
And your accounts and spending, with no bank connection needed.

31
00:02:28.413 --> 00:02:33.324
Because everything is in one place, one page can show everyone who has access to your data.

32
00:02:34.834 --> 00:02:37.646
Here, some files are open to anyone with the link.

33
00:02:37.646 --> 00:02:39.614
One click makes them private again.

34
00:02:40.464 --> 00:02:43.133
Bob has had access to some files since October.

35
00:02:43.133 --> 00:02:46.995
You can see exactly what he can reach, and take it back at any time.

36
00:02:47.845 --> 00:02:54.716
Underneath, the suite is built on open standards: Solid, and the W3C's work on Linked Web Storage.

37
00:02:55.565 --> 00:03:02.618
The code is open source, as more than seventy reusable packages, so anyone can build their own apps on the same pods.

38
00:03:03.468 --> 00:03:12.246
Next comes a personal agent that asks before it acts, mobile apps, and more apps reaching feature parity with the tools you use today.

39
00:03:13.096 --> 00:03:17.772
Try the demo for yourself at solid dash suite dot vercel dot app.
